Dialogue: 1,0:01:58.61,0:02:04.59,Episode Titles,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fsp2\fad(800,800)\pos(360,190)\bord1.6}...The Footsteps of Spring.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.10,0:23:12.10,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}Your smile falls in that space
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.84,0:23:20.36,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}between the things I've lost and the things I've gained.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.55,0:23:26.36,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}It seems as if I could reach it, but I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.15,0:23:31.81,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}It's not as if I can fly...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.11,0:23:38.41,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}Even though I only wanted to make you smile...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.21,0:23:49.36,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}What purpose do they serve, these useless wings of mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.13,0:24:00.34,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}All I can do is smile by your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.98,0:24:07.39,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}I wonder if it's okay to only warm your heart
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.47,0:24:12.21,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}when, at the very least, I want to envelop you in warmth.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.63,0:24:19.70,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}Have you noticed? I want to embrace you with my wings.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.50,0:24:27.84,Ending,,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(200,200)\be1\org(0,0)}And now, I am able to smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.08,0:24:29.94,Episode Titles,,0000,0000,0000,,{\bord1.5\be1\fs25\fad(400,0)\c&H111111&\3c&HFFFFFF&\pos(434,250)}Next
